KG42.register("clusters-53c998b75bbd78b6fb1cadf5",{"id":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v142-d-K004","paper":"22-decentralized_flexibility_markets","label":"Linkage from agreed contract prices to payment obligations and interpretation of case revenue","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K004","label":"Linkage from agreed contract prices to payment obligations and interpretation of case revenue","market_meaning":"For a flexibility contract already agreed between buyer and seller, the contract price determines the buyer's payment obligation to the seller. In the case, the correspondence between DSO expenditure and participating entities' revenue, no revenue for non-participants, and higher revenue under high battery degradation cost are retained as qualified results; the complete interface from bargaining state to payment amount remains to be clarified.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["participation","coordination","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"General payment semantics apply only to the same contract that has been agreed. The contract price record in R003 can be associated with the settlement input of R007 only under this condition; buyer and seller bids are not directly equivalent to an agreed amount. The revenue descriptions in R001 and R007 are limited to the corresponding case; the revenue change in Case Study B does not constitute a general cost-compensation formula.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The payment obligation has an independent agreed-contract input, payer and receipt result, and is therefore assembled independently of price formation. The shared pricing and coordination chains are used to explain the price input; the shared participation chain only explains the background of zero revenue in the specific case.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries per-contract payment obligations and the qualified case revenue result."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the semantics of an agreed contract price that is unique per transaction, without separately owning the price-formation rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"References the price record in the contract tuple, retains its role in the bargaining stage, and conditionally associates it with the final settlement input."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"context","rationale":"Only provides the non-participation background for the zero revenue of prosumers 46–55 in the case, and does not become a premise of the general payment obligation."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-L011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::param_contract_price","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e13","v141-b-g02-e24"],"rationale":"The source interprets the price of an agreed contract as the amount the seller receives from the buyer, so there is a functional linkage between the pricing result and the payment obligation. This connection is conditional on an existing agreed contract and does not fabricate proof that bilateral bids are consistent."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L012","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::param_contract_price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"The contract-tuple price becomes a payment input after the same contract is finally agreed. This interface retains the operational-variable role in bargaining and the fixed-input role in settlement, and does not interpret all temporary bids as payments that have occurred."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-L013","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-E11"],"rationale":"The resource-lack and non-participation record of the same case is linked with the explanation of zero revenue for these entities in the revenue result; only the result for this specified group is retained, and no general settlement constraint is added."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O008","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E10"],"rationale":"Both references refer to local contract pricing in the same mechanism, serving respectively as a pricing result and a payment input; the display representative does not change the content of each chain, nor is it interpreted as a uniform market price."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-O009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R007::theta::param_contract_price"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e23"],"rationale":"Only when referencing the same final agreed contract do the two correspond to its price component. The local roles of bargaining operational variable and settlement parameter remain different; unagreed contracts and buyer and seller bids do not fall within this same-quantity judgment."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G014","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R007 treats the contract price as the receipt amount, whereas the case's price-adjustment step uses an energy unit-price unit. C does not clarify the mapping from the terminal bid to the agreed contract price, nor does it explain the monetary conversion between the relevant bid and the energy quantity of each contract, so the complete price-to-payment interface is not yet closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-T002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R007::theta::param_contract_price","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e29"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-flexibility-contract","v141-b-g02-p01"],"required_work":"Check the source conventions for contract amount, unit energy price and contract energy quantity, and have the upstream clarify the final price interface; retain the conditional semantics that the agreed amount determines payment, and do not calculate or add conversion formulas on one's own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G015","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R007-C002 to C004 are case revenue descriptions and lack a revenue-aggregation definition and a citable payment-balance expression. Higher degradation cost corresponding to higher revenue cannot be used to establish an exact compensation ratio or a general budget-balance rule.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e29","v141-b-g03-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If quantitative accounting is needed, the upstream should supplement definitions and source expressions for revenue, cost and payment aggregation; currently the descriptive case results and their conditions are retained and are not elevated to a general settlement algorithm."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G016","category":"unverified_source","description":"Payment semantics, price-object associations and the case revenue interpretation all depend on B excerpts that remain unverified and have not undergone independent source review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E08","v141-b-g01-E10","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e23","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e29","v141-b-g02-e30","v141-b-g03-E11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the contract price unit, bilateral payment semantics and case revenue scope; object associations remain candidate in nature and do not change the source status."}]},"rule_refs":["22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R007","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R006","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R003","22-decentralized_flexibility_markets::v141-c-R001"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-10be07664c6496b7","COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","COMP-739917e3869e45a6","COMP-75186ff50e007d27","KG31-5be8ae1142e7d54c"]});
